WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 5: Tell Me How.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.920
Unit 5 turns you into a writer of instructions.

3
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:12.300
You will take apart a Somali recipe for
bariis to see how a title, a materials list,

4
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.720
numbered steps and tips work together,
and you will learn the zero conditional,

5
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.180
the pattern that explains what happens every single time.

6
00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.640
Alongside the recipe you will read “The Memory Wall”,

7
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.180
a story about a class who learn to
communicate what matters to them.

8
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.380
By the end you will have planned, drafted,

9
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.780
tested and revised your own set of instructions
that somebody else can genuinely follow.

10
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:41.400
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:47.700
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
read procedural and instructional texts closely,

12
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.600
naming their key features and explaining
how the structure helps the reader.

13
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.360
You will also recognise imperative verbs
such as rinse, stir, place and measure,

14
00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.800
and open your own written steps with them.

15
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.520
You will also identify and use time
connectives such as first, next, then,

16
00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.020
after that and finally to sequence steps clearly.

17
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.760
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

18
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:17.700
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: criticise,
interfere, interrupt, accompany, assemble, namely.

19
00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:23.480
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

20
00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.000
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

21
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:34.260
The reading sequence includes What Makes
Instructions Work and How to Make Bariis: Spiced Rice.

22
00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:36.220
Read actively.

23
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.340
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.260
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:49.960
The first language focus is What the Zero Conditional Is For.

26
00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.700
The zero conditional describes
results that follow every single time.

27
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.380
Scientists reach for it to state facts,

28
00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:03.060
and instruction writers reach for it to explain
what happens when a step is done properly or skipped.

29
00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:09.180
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

30
00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:14.900
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: The Instruction Game (Pairs).

31
00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:20.260
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

32
00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.640
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

33
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.040
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

34
00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:28.960
You are ready to begin.

35
00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:35.580
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

36
00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.240
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

37
00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:45.820
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
